new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..b63f1ec6f0263e356eb46393166a686fc9f3dcae
--- /dev/null
+++ b/REVIEW.md
@@ -0,0 +1,532 @@
+# Independent adversarial audit: 81-numerical-letter-grade
+
+## Executive decision
+
+The candidate contains several genuine, freshly reproducible K reachability
+proofs, but it does not contain a proof of the requested function for an
+arbitrary input list. Its only top-level symbolic theorems cover the empty list
+and a list of length one; the only longer top-level theorem is the single
+concrete prompt example. The two loop-step claims establish one iteration at a
+time but no claim states or proves the arbitrary-list result. The unused
+`expectedGrades` function makes this omission especially visible.
+
+There is also a real generated-semantics mismatch. `semantic.k` assigns exact
+decimal rational meanings to Python float literals. When a runtime Python float
+is represented by its actual exact binary ratio, the K execution disagrees with
+both Python implementations at intended threshold inputs 3.7, 2.7, and 1.3.
+Thus the successful claims concern a narrower exact-decimal abstraction, with
+no proved connection to the real Python float execution.
+
+These are material adequacy and real-program-model failures. Successful fresh
+`#Top` results and a successful non-vacuity probe do not repair them.
+
+## 1. Input and provenance integrity
+
+### Mode boundary
+
+The rendered mode is `GENERATED_SEMANTICS`. `/reference` contains exactly the
+three declared trusted regular files:
+
+- `/reference/canonical.py`
+- `/reference/prompt.py`
+- `/reference/py2mpy.py`
+
+`/reference/reference-semantics` is absent, as required. There is no
+infrastructure-mode contradiction, so a candidate verdict is appropriate.
+See [01-integrity.log](evidence/01-integrity.log).
+
+### Candidate artifact integrity
+
+All candidate source and provenance artifacts required for this audit are
+present as regular files: `run-input.json`, `metrics.json`, `codex-last.txt`,
+`codex-output.log`, `prompt.py`, `py2mpy.py`, `semantic.k`, `solution.py`,
+`solution.mpy`, `spec.k`, `verification.k`, and `prove.sh`. The structured
+trace is present at
+`/candidate/codex-trace/2026/07/22/rollout-2026-07-22T05-49-57-019f8972-4f98-7280-a36c-d3732b1bc74c.jsonl`.
+None of these required artifacts is missing, mistyped, or symlinked.
+
+The candidate prompt and translator compare byte-identically with their
+trusted mounted versions:
+
+- prompt SHA-256:
+  `489ff1f658e105a21a1e28c105082983a77af3a6b0576d9cdfb43745de1b507c`
+- translator SHA-256:
